From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t3code-customize <t3code-customize@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:22:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Local: show a proxy's pooled limits in the thread details
 card

A Claude instance that talks to a custom endpoint (a CLI proxy) cannot read
subscription limits itself, so the thread details card only said
"Limits: Unavailable" while the Usage page showed the proxy's accounts. The
card now falls back to those accounts for the same driver, pooled the way the
Usage page summarises them, with a tooltip naming the source and account
count. Instances on their own subscription keep showing their own limits or
their own failure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
